//! flags: -p ssa

// A loop's flag set to the same constant in two arms, one of them nested,
// is not that constant on the way round: the latch hands the header what
// the header already carries, and the definitions analysis has to say so.
//
// `descend` is apps/pbrt's light-tree descent (render.bonsai, bvh_descend)
// in miniature: `done` is set in the leaf arm and, inside the interior
// arm, in the arm of zero importance; the third path leaves it as the
// header had it. After promotion the merge before the latch takes `done`
// from the leaf arm's edge, `true`, and from the interior arm's own merge
// of `true` with the header's `done`. What to read for: the latch's jump
// to the header hands `done`, the merge's argument, and not `(bool)1`.
//
// Until 2026-10-19 it handed the constant. The simplifier's constant rule
// (SSA/Simplify.cpp, substitute_threaded_arguments) asks the definitions
// analysis (SSA/Definitions.cpp) what every edge hands; asked about a
// block inside the interior arm first, the analysis followed the name to
// the header, round the latch to the merge, and into the interior arm's
// merge, whose edge back to the header's own `done` it skipped as carried
// round unchanged -- answering `true`, provisionally. The merge before the
// latch then saw `true` from both edges; the skip was a level below it, so
// nothing marked its answer provisional, and `true` was memoized for the
// question that came after about the latch itself. The descent stopped
// at the root: any scene with more than one light sampled only the
// first. tests/bonsai/correctness/llvm/constant-argument-provisional runs
// it: descend(5, 10) is 5, and was -1.
func [[export]] descend(n : i32, stop : i32) -> i32 {
    i : mut i32 = 0;
    chosen : mut i32 = -1;
    done : mut bool = false;
    while !done {
        if i >= n {
            chosen = i;
            done = true;
        } else {
            if i == stop {
                done = true;
            } else {
                i = i + 1;
            }
        }
    }
    return chosen;
}
